BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:iac-bc-ai-builders-fellowship-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T204058Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260821
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260822
SUMMARY:Deadline: AI Builders Fellowship 2026 (Internet Archive Canada x BC
  + AI)
DESCRIPTION:A $5\,000 fellowship to spend six weeks turning a very large Ca
 nadian public archive into something new. THE MATERIAL: Internet Archive C
 anada's Government Publications collection\, part of the Democracy's Libra
 ry project\, holding over 104\,000 text items\, roughly 22.1 million scann
 ed pages and about 48.25 TB of Canadian public-record material\, browsable
  at archive.org/details/governmentpublications. WHAT TO BUILD: deliberatel
 y open-ended. The call names a search tool that answers a real question wi
 th page-level citations\, a timeline tracing one policy across decades of 
 government language\, and a sonic or visual piece built from archival mate
 rial\, but explicitly invites work nobody has thought of yet. The requirem
 ents are that it is useful\, that it is imaginative\, and that the code is
  open source when it is done. ORIGIN: the fellowship came out of conversat
 ions between BC + AI's Kris Kruger and IAC executive director Andrea Mills
  about treating a public archive as material for new work rather than only
  something to preserve. IAC brings the archive\, BC + AI brings a communit
 y of builders used to working in public. ELIGIBILITY: anyone\, anywhere in
  the world\; one builder is selected. APPLICATION: a specific project desc
 ription grounded in the collection\, a phase-by-phase work plan for the si
 x weeks\, and a success metric\, submitted at bc-ai.ca/fellowship/apply. K
 EY DATES: applications close 21 August 2026 at 11:59pm Pacific\; fellow se
 lected by 31 August\; build runs 1 September to mid-October\; showcase at 
 Futureproof Festival in Vancouver on 28 October 2026 if the project is rea
 dy.\n\nOrganisation: Internet Archive Canada (IAC) in partnership with BC 
 + AI\nLocation: Remote\, open to builders anywhere in the world. Optional 
 in-person showcase at Futureproof Festival in Vancouver\, Canada on 28 Oct
 ober 2026 if the project is ready.\nAward: $5\,000 award for one selected 
 builder. No application fee.\nDuration: Six-week build\, 1 September to mi
 d-October 2026\, remote\, with support from BC + AI throughout\n\nMore: ht
 tps://bc-ai.ca/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://bc-ai.ca/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\, open to builders anywhere in the world. Optional in-perso
 n showcase at Futureproof Festival in Vancouver\, Canada on 28 October 202
 6 if the project is ready.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:video-pool-matr-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T204058Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:Deadline: Video Pool: Media Art + Technology Residency (MATR) 2027
DESCRIPTION:Video Pool's Media Art + Technology Residency supports experime
 ntal\, independent\, technology-based work. The selected artist or artists
  develop a new project (or adapt and transform an existing one) in direct 
 response to the intimate scale and specific character of the Poolside Gall
 ery\, culminating in an exhibition there. The call is deliberately open on
  medium: video\, sound\, installation\, digital media\, performance\, inte
 ractive technologies\, expanded cinema and interdisciplinary practices are
  all welcome. VP asks proposals to speak clearly to your practice\, the qu
 estions\, materials or ideas that drive the work\, and how that work might
  grow\, shift or take new form inside the gallery. It is explicitly intere
 sted in expansive proposals\, work that pushes past the gallery's four wal
 ls to engage its surrounding spaces (hallways\, windows\, projection wall)
  or that reimagines what the gallery itself can hold\, and in projects tha
 t engage technology as a creative\, critical\, aesthetic or socio-politica
 l tool. Priority is given to artists from equity-seeking communities whose
  practices contribute to the advancement of experimental media arts. Resid
 ents get full access to VP's available equipment\, facilities and technica
 l resources throughout the residency\, and applicants are encouraged to re
 view the equipment and facilities list before proposing. ELIGIBILITY: open
  to VP members (this is a member submission call)\; no nationality restric
 tion is stated\, but the residency and exhibition are in person in Winnipe
 g. APPLICATION: artist bio (1\,500 characters)\, headshot\, description of
  your artistic practice (3\,000 characters)\, project proposal for MATR (3
 \,000 characters)\, equipment and facility needs (750 characters)\, descri
 ption of how you would use the space (750 characters)\, CV\, up to five im
 ages (optional) and up to two video or documentation links. Submit via the
  online form at videopool.org/matr-2027-application/ by 30 August 2026\; a
 lternative submission formats can be arranged by contacting Emma (emma@vid
 eopool.org) or Iyunade (iyunade@videopool.org). General enquiries: info@vi
 deopool.org\, 204-949-9134.\n\nOrganisation: Video Pool Media Arts Centre\
 nLocation: In person at Video Pool Media Arts Centre and its Poolside Gall
 ery\, 221-100 Arthur Street\, Winnipeg\, Manitoba R3B 1H3\, Canada.\nAward
 : CAD 2\,250 artist fee\, covering both the residency period and the subse
 quent Poolside Gallery exhibition. Residents also get full access to VP's 
 equipment\, facilities and technical resources\; the Poolside Gallery itse
 lf is equipped with two projectors and four speakers. Applicants must be V
 P members\, so a membership is purchased separately\, but there is no sepa
 rate application fee.\nDuration: Up to two months to develop and install t
 he project\, including one month of dedicated access to the Poolside Galle
 ry. Residency takes place in Winter 2027\; exhibition dates TBD.\n\nMore: 
 https://videopool.org/media-arts-technology-residency-2027-call-for-applic
 ations/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://videopool.org/media-arts-technology-residency-2027-call-for-app
 lications/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:In person at Video Pool Media Arts Centre and its Poolside Gallery
 \, 221-100 Arthur Street\, Winnipeg\, Manitoba R3B 1H3\, Canada.
END:VEVENT
